            {
              "id": "56a16b49-45d9-40a3-88f8-2c2e3f84fdbc",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Sport &amp; Religion</strong></em><strong> i</strong>s a collection of essays edited by Shirl J. Hoffman, published by Human Kinetics, January 1, 1992."
            },
            {
              "id": "7666a754-5b20-4e78-a8d6-76774d18dbba",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "2efa47c0-6f4e-4fc9-8b53-98073b63360e",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>Hoffman has compiled a provocative collection of articles and written insightful introductions to the four sections of the book: sport as religion (and sport is not a religion); sport as religious experience; religion in sport; and sport, religion, and ethics. Of interest to a broad audience; the similarities, differences, and interplay offer unique windows into American culture and the collective social conscience.</em>"
            }
          ]
